  {
    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "Agree with this. Scheduled local Codex sessions that email you or message you offer a lot more control over important tasks because you can change the context and prompts. I still enjoy using a Dot for many tasks, but it is not a replacement. https://x.com/krishnanrohit/status/2116323804695966093?a=A_RcI2tdDKt_VYbF3y4&s=20",
    "quoted_tweet": {
      "author": "rohit",
      "username": "krishnanrohit",
      "text": "@emollick For many of the use cases, I've gone back to starting to use Codex locally precisely because of this. I know when I can and should intervene."
    },
