    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "The market for software migration from legacy systems has been limited to $30B a year or so because migration is very expensive and maintenance is easier. Talking to older firms, there is a real backlog of scoped cheaper migration projects being unlocked by AI surprisingly fast",
